proof.text:
For a basic proper or open letter $A$ put $N_A=A\mathcal RM$. The generator transpose identity and the reduction/limit triangle identity give
$$\mathcal L(r_A)u_{A_{\rm int}M}
=\mathcal L(e_{N_A})\mathcal L\mathcal R(d_A^{-1})u_{A_{\rm int}M}
=\mathcal L(e_{N_A})u_{\mathcal LN_A}d_A^{-1}=d_A^{-1}.$$
For a proper $p$, denote the canonical direct-image/limit comparison by $b_{p,N}:Rp_*\mathcal LN\to\mathcal LS_pN$. Its normalization gives $d_{p,M}^{-1}=b_{p,\mathcal RM}Rp_*(u_M)$. Indeed both are the specified direct-image/limit comparison applied after the input completion unit. This also follows in constant coordinates from the one-letter formula $a_p=\mathcal L^{\mathcal T}(q_p)\eta$ and its asserted agreement with the canonical direct-image/limit comparison.
